{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386204-help-with-a-tremere-sourcebook","id":1386204,"title":"Help with a Tremere sourcebook","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-06T16:30:43-07:00","id":1386204,"title":"Help with a Tremere sourcebook","content":"Hello. <br /> <br /> A couple years ago I was reading about the Tremere in a book - dont remember which one - and I ran into a paragraph describing their magic. That paragraph left me thinking: &quot;holy shit...this describes hermetic magic muuuuuch better than any Mage book!&quot;. Now I'm running a Mage Chronicle and one of my players decided to make an Hermetic mage. She's a newbie and that paragraph was all I needed to explain the type of magic Hermetics do without using the &quot;Harry Potter&quot; comparison (which is useless anyway). I just cant find the damn book... <br /> <br /> By any chance, do any of you know what is the book Im talking about? I know the reference is suuuuuper vague, but I wanted to try my luck anyway. <br /> <br /> Thanx","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T16:39:41-07:00","id":1386207,"title":"","content":"Either Clanbook Tremere Revised or House of Secrets (a Dark Ages book describing the Ceoris chantry)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/defa